{
  "resume": "=== Leyli Hernandez - Resume.pdf ===\nMAY 24, 2009 \u2022 U.S. CITIZEN \u2022 99-22 42ND AVE, BASEMENT, CORONA, UNITED \nSTATES, 11368 \u2022 leyyhdzzz@gmail.com \u2022 (347)453-8142 \n\nLEYLI  HERNANDEZ \n\nABOUT ME \n\nMy name is Leyli Hernandez, 17 years old. I\u2019ve grown up and lived in Queens and am very \npassionate about helping my community in any way, anytime. I am constantly assisting in \nany event which has allowed me to be very engaging towards others whenever I get the \nopportunity. I love to stay physically active and always have something to do. I am always \ndown to try new things and expand my horizons. \n\nVOLUNTEERING  HISTORY \n\n\u25cf \n\n\u25cf \n\nI spend most of the weekends or afterschool hours volunteering with Elmhurst \nCommunity Partnership(ECP) which is a non-profit organization that provides free \nsports clubs, social groups, community assistance, community events and other \nactivities. \nI am also the Co-Chair of the Executive Board of another non-profit company I work \nwith called SPEAKHIRE. SPEAKHIRE works with Middle Schools, High Schools, and \nColleges to help students work on their leadership skills, career paths, and connects \nthese students with professionals based on their career interests. I am also chair to \nthe Media committee, and work with planning our monthly events to help them run \nsmoother. \n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\fSKILLS \n\nTeam Leadership (Experienced), Community Engagement (Experienced), Problem Solving \n(Experienced), Social Media Management (Experienced), Quick Learner, Organized, Public \nSpeaking (Experienced). \n\nEDUCATION \n\nHIGH SCHOOL \n\n40-11 28th St, Astoria, NY 11101  \n\nCurrently a Junior Student-Athlete at Academy of American Studies High \nSchool as I am part of the Varsity Girls Flag Football team  \n\nLANGUAGES \n\nEnglish (Native), Spanish (Highly proficient).",
